course: dictionary
lesson: 340
title: Announcements
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An announcement is a message told to lots of people at once, to share news or information. «At the gate you listen for announcements and check the board, because gates and times can change.» The word listen tells you that announcements are often spoken, so people can hear them.
explain: Use the words around a new word to work out its meaning. «Passengers keep to the passenger decks and listen to safety announcements.» Safety announcements must be messages about staying safe, so an announcement is a message for everyone. Try your meaning in the sentence: "listen to safety messages" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: When someone makes an announcement, they tell people something officially, so everyone should know it. Phrases like «an important announcement» show that the news matters.
fact: An announcement is a public message that tells people some news or information.
fact: Announcements are often made in assembly, over a loudspeaker, or at stations and airports.
fact: To make an announcement means to tell people something officially.
fact: «Safety announcements» on a ferry tell passengers how to stay safe.
fact: In «Alice in Wonderland», the White Rabbit is the herald, an officer who reads announcements.
exercise: «At the gate you listen for announcements and check the board.» What is an announcement? | A kind of gate made of wood | A ticket for a train | *A message told to people to share news or information | A quiet whisper between friends
exercise: «The White Rabbit is the herald, the officer who reads announcements.» Who reads announcements in this story? | *The herald, an officer who reads announcements | A mouse who hides under the table | The Queen's cook | A ferry captain
exercise: Which of these is most like an announcement? | A bird singing quietly in a tree | A child drawing a picture at home | *The school tells everyone over the loudspeaker that sports day is on Friday | Two friends sharing a secret
test: «Passengers keep to the passenger decks and listen to safety announcements.» Why do passengers listen to safety announcements? | To hear a song | To learn how to stay safe | *Both A and B are wrong, they listen for fun | To find out what the cook is making
test: «An important announcement» is a message that is what? | Whispered only to one person | Silly and short | *Official and worth listening to | A kind of ticket
exam: Ella hears, «Please listen, we have an important announcement.» What should she do, and why? | Shout over the speaker, because she has news | Cover her ears, because announcements are too loud | *Listen carefully, because the message gives people news or information | Walk away, because announcements are always boring
